A1. This one has just gone under new management. ~ BRIDEGROOM
A10. A buddy. ~ PARD
A14. This used to hang around the ladies in the gay nineties. ~ LACE
A15. A paper weight. ~ OUNCE
A16. What some singers do to get to the top. ~ SLUR
A17. This man tries to run the building and some people were very much put out. ~ AGENT
A19. This one always takes its honey on its flying trips. ~ BEE
A20. This was written about Springtime. ~ ODE
A21. This has manly characteristics. ~ HE
A22. This poor thing hangs over the sink all of the time. ~ TAP
A24. These were onee a fine swimming school until someone canned them. ~ SARDINES
A28. This is what Ireland is to-day. ~ ISLE
A30. Something attractive a wife sees about her husband when he is convalescing. ~ NURSE
A31. Introducing an alternative. ~ OR
A33. The very latest reports from this are "they have stopped selling short." ~ STYLE
A35. An uncle who is boss of the biggest business in the world. ~ SAM
A36. Only the first person can precede this. ~ AM
A37. This is what they have when good fellows get together. ~ PARTY
A39. What puzzle makers often become. ~ BATTY
A41. A brotherly fellow. ~ FRA
A42. Holiday decorations. ~ TIES
A43. A raid. ~ FORAY
A44. This one made a quick turnover after going into the market. ~ COOK
A45. Humorist without any humor. ~ IST
A46. These often become beautiful women. ~ GOWNS
A47. A popular song. ~ THEME
A48. This is the way the measles start. ~ ME
A49. Just because. ~ FOR
A50. That last lingering look. ~ STARE
A52. This was all that was left of his dollar after he took his doll out. ~ AR
A53. This is some land. ~ TRACT
A55. A rough rider. ~ ERIE
A56. These have started many a young person on the downward path. ~ SCOOTERS
A59. This travels with a fast crowd. ~ CAR
A60. An expression of surprise. ~ OH
A62. When they make a Ford do this it might move ahead of a Cadillac. ~ TOW
A63. This is foaming over with good spirits. ~ ALE
A65. An unintelligible speech. ~ LINGO
A67. It took the whole office force to carry this out. ~ IDEA
A69. These used to be found at matinees. ~ IDOLS
A71. This one owns the richest banks in Africa and runs over there every year. ~ NILE
A72. This has been in the penitentiary for a long time. ~ CELL
A73. This is what dad calls modern. ~ NEWFANGLED

D1. This is the bunk. ~ BLAH
D2. Dad became very angry when he fell into this. ~ RAGE
D3. This has a melting disposition. ~ ICE
D4. These will bore you to tears. ~ DENTISTS
D5. A forward movement in the traffic regulations. ~ GO
D6. The first beat of the drum. ~ RUB
D7. These are the most singular things in the world. ~ ONES
D8. A wet situation that can never be settled. ~ OCEAN
D9. A personal pronoun. ~ ME
D10. After words. (abbr.) ~ PS
D11. The way the Statue of Liberty stands. ~ ALONE
D12. The kind of people who have a lot of push. ~ RUDE
D13. This is what real Worth is in Paris. ~ DRESSMAKER
D18. The kind of pies that mother used to make. ~ TASTY
D23. To work steadily. ~ PLY
D25. The way an old Ford looks. ~ RUSTY
D26. An old style truck. ~ DRAY
D27. A distinctive doctrine. ~ ISM
D29. This kind of grease will remove that ring around the tub. ~ ELBOW
D31. "Pop, what's an optimist ?" ~ OPTIMISTIC
D32. If you can't get this from the boss ask the elevator boy. ~ RAISE
D34. This is what dad does from Monday morning until Saturday night. ~ EARNS
D36. This is what they got over the air from Mocha and Java. ~ AROMA
D38. To soak. ~ RET
D40. The proof of the pudding. ~ TASTE
D41. This will never agree with you. ~ FOE
D43. The police are on to this. ~ FORCE
D44. This is what Paris was doing when We arrived. ~ CHEERING
D46. There are many pounds of butter in this. ~ GOAT
D47. There are always two sides to this. ~ TRIAL
D49. A backward movement. ~ FRO
D51. There are no angles to this. ~ ARC
D53. This is going to be a great help for the wets. ~ TOWEL
D54. One of the Smith boys. ~ TRADE
D57. You will need a key for this. ~ CODE
D58. These kind of people don't get very far. ~ SLOW
D60. You can't do this with your eyes shut. ~ OGLE
D61. This is what they did for the farmers. ~ HOED
D64. A naughty imp. ~ ELF
D66. This means nothing to us. ~ NIL
D68. A loser in last year's derby. ~ AL
D69. Half an inch. ~ IN
